[gt4157a@prism.gatech.EDU (Alexander Barton) writes:]
[] 1.  When you Quaff from a fountain and "You 
[]     are refreshed by the cool drought," does that
[]     mean that you've gained an intrinsic?

No, it means you are refreshed by the cool draught, which is
inconsequential. Gaining/losing intrinsics is usually accompanied
by a special feeling (i.e. "you feel very jumpy" when you gain
intrinsic teleport).

[] 2.  Can someone post info about then geography of 
[]     the dungeon?  Like:  Where's 'Vlad's castle and
[]     where's Hell.  I suspect that they don't have 
[]     fixed places but that they do have a fixed 
[]     order. (Yes?)

{{{a mild spoiler warning about hell but read this anyway}}}

You're not gonna believe this but hell is at the bottom at the
dungeon and extends over a dozen or more levels (nh3.0 pl7). Hell
contains 3 levels which are known as Vlad's towers and also contains
a level where the Wizard of Yendor lives. Also, there are levels
where named demons have taken up residence, living as though they
were the Wizard of Yendor, but they're only imitators. Vlad's location
and the Wizard's are random in hell.

Because hell is at the bottom of things there are no stairwells down,
however in Vlad's tower there are down ladders. You can imagine that
hell is a very hot place so be prepared, intrinsically.

